> simply adds the indices of those columns and returns the 7th column as a
> result.
>
> Is that really an example of something that is an intended use of the
> evaluation of the column names, or might it be better for that to throw an
> error?
>
> (It would be neat if select(mtcars,disp + hp) returned the sum of the
> columns, but I'm guessing that's not the intended use for select())
